# Booking — Cron Resource Occupancy Retention Purge Trigger
# TD40 Story 2: publishes the cron-resource-occupancy-retention-purge trigger, dispatched to
# ResourceOccupancyRetentionPurgeTriggerHandler. In production, Cloud Scheduler publishes the same
# trigger directly to Pub/Sub daily at 03:00 UTC — this endpoint is the local/manual trigger path
# only, protected by the global InternalApiGuard (X-Internal-Key), not PubSubPushGuard.
# Response is { ok: true } once the trigger is published — it does not wait for the job to
# finish. Requires the Pub/Sub emulator running (pnpm infra:up).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev

@baseUrl = {{backendUrl}}

### POST /cron/resource-occupancy-retention-purge — publish the daily resource_occupancy retention-purge trigger
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/resource-occupancy-retention-purge
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

###
